e absolutely right that it “seems like a lot more.” But the actual mass of bean material per serving is still exquisitely small. The specks are an optical and tactile flourish, not a nutritional or flavor-based mountain of bean. It’s the most brilliant trick in vanilla marketing: a sprinkle of seeds that makes us think we’re swimming in whole pods.
